{{Quote|Is that a bounty puck? Is that me?|[[The Fledgling Mythrol|The Mythrol]], to [[Din Djarin]]|<ref name="The Mandalorian 1">[[The Mandalorian 1|''The Mandalorian'' 1]]</ref>}}
'''Holopucks''',<ref name="Holopuck DB">{{Databank|holopuck|holopuck}}</ref> also known as '''holographic pucks''',<ref name="Star Wars Book">''[[The Star Wars Book]]''</ref> '''data pucks''',<ref name="Infiltration">{{TBB|Infiltration (episode)}}</ref> or referred to as '''bounty pucks''',<ref name="Mando1" /> were a small, simple [[Hologram|holographic]] device utilized by the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]] that identified a quarry.

==Description==
[[File:Bounty_puck.png|thumb|left|250px|A bounty puck showing The Mythrol.]]
Holopucks displayed a holographic image of the quarry accompanied by the word "WANTED" in [[Aurebesh]] as well as listing the details of a bounty: the amount of credits offered, the circumstances (or crimes) that warranted the bounty, the operational jurisdiction allowed for pursuit, and the specific conditions required to collect. <ref name="Star Wars Book" /> A puck provided information that when combined with the use of a [[tracking fob]], allowed [[Bounty hunter|Guild members]] to hunt their quarry to the edge of [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Holopuck DB" />

==History==
The [[Galactic Empire]] maintained a highly encrypted target register that was listed on holopucks carried by [[Clone X trooper]]s.<ref name="Infiltration" />

In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Mando Date">{{MandoDate|1}}</ref> the Guild on [[Nevarro]] handed holopucks out to their members. By taking the puck, the hunter accepted the bounty.<ref name="Mando1" /> 

{{Tech-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Holopucks first appeared in [[Chapter 1: The Mandalorian|Chapter 1]] of the [[2019]] [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'',<ref name="Mando1" /> which aired on [[November 12]], 2019.<ref name="DTCI">{{WebCite|url=https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf|text=The Mandalorian Media Kit|work=[https://dtcimedia.disney.com Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International]|archivedate=20230315011507}}</ref> The holopuck was later identified as such in its [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] entry on [[StarWars.com]].<ref name="Holopuck DB" />

